id: pm-gh1769
title: "GH-1769: the extension test harness accepts universal output controls on non-read commands that the native CLI refuses before dispatch"
description: "GH-1769 (filed 2026-11-22, reproduced on 2026.11.22). createExtensionTestHarness().runCommand and runRegisteredCommandForTest accept universal output controls (outputBudget, outputLimit, outputInclude, outputCursor, and the other canonical read-output keys) on an extension command that declares no read_output. The native CLI refuses the same invocation before dispatch: pm probe echo --output-budget 1 --json exits 2 with \"Universal output controls apply only to read commands; probe echo is not a read surface.\" The native guard is validateReadOutputOptions (src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts), called in the CLI preAction hook (src/cli/main.ts) and in PmClient.run dispatchAction (src/sdk/runtime.ts) with the active extension registrations published. The harness (src/sdk/testing.ts runRegisteredCommandForTest) never calls it, so a package test passes for an invocation every real agent sees refused. This is the parity gap GH-1729 (pm-gh1729, closed) set out to close for read-output results; it did not cover pre-dispatch admission of the controls themselves. Duplicate check: searched \"extension test harness universal output controls read surface\"; pm-gh1729 and pm-extension-read-output-controls are closed and own result admission and the read_output opt-in, nothing owns the pre-dispatch control refusal in the harness."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: extensions,"gh:1769",read-output,sdk,testing
created_at: "2026-11-23T08:22:13.674Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-23T11:57:25.824Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-23T09:39:58.815Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-23T09:39:58.815Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "A harness call to a non-read extension command with any universal output control fails with the native refusal's exit code and message; A command that declares read_output keeps accepting the controls, and malformed control values are refused as natively; A parity spec runs the same invocation through the harness and the built CLI and compares the refusals"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: low
confidence: high
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "runRegisteredCommandForTest (src/sdk/testing.ts) runs the shared validateReadOutputOptions admission before the handler inside an isolated runtime holding the activation's registrations, reading controls from global and options; a hand-built registry is not checked. The native refusal is now typed read_output_surface_unsupported (exit 2, same message, details.output_option_keys) and READ_OUTPUT_SURFACE_UNSUPPORTED_CODE is exported. docs/SDK.md and docs/READ_OUTPUT_CONTRACTS.md document both."
expected_result: "runCommand refuses universal output controls on a non-read extension command with the same code, exit and message as native dispatch, a read_output command keeps accepting them, malformed values are refused"
actual_result: "The parity spec compares the built CLI and the harness for four controls through global and options (same code, exit 2, message, no handler run), --output-format yaml in both, and probe report accepting --output-limit; harness-parity covers the hybrid comments surface and the hand-built registry skip"
