comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-23T08:47:01.040Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence (2026-11-23). runRegisteredCommandForTest (src/sdk/testing.ts) now calls the shared validateReadOutputOptions before the handler runs, inside an isolated extension runtime that holds the activation's registrations, so resolveReadOutputSurface sees the command's read_output declaration exactly as CLI preAction and PmClient.run dispatchAction do. Controls are read from both places a harness caller can put them: global (outputInclude, outputLimit, outputBudget, outputFormat, outputSession, outputCursor, outputRowContract) and options (camel or snake keys). A hand-built registry carries no declarations and is not checked, matching admitRegisteredReadOutputResult.\n\nThe native refusal was untyped (command_failed). It now carries the stable code read_output_surface_unsupported (exit 2, same message) with details.output_option_keys, required and why; READ_OUTPUT_SURFACE_UNSUPPORTED_CODE is exported. Probed on the built CLI: pm create Task --title x --output-row-contract refuses with the new code, so output-row-contract reaches the native check through command options and including it in the harness keeps parity.\n\nParity spec (direct-caller-option-contract.integration.spec.ts): for --output-budget, --output-limit, --output-include and --output-cursor the built CLI refuses probe option with read_output_surface_unsupported, and the harness refuses the same invocation through global and through options with the same code, exit 2 and message; the handler's run counter shows no run happened; --output-format yaml is refused with the native message in both; probe report (declares read_output) accepts --output-limit in both. harness-parity.spec.ts adds the extended native hybrid surface (comments with add plus outputLimit refuses read_output_mutation_conflict) and the hand-built registry skip.\n"
  "2026-11-23T10:16:00.116Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 1 on PR #1772 (Codex gpt-6.2-sol, 2026-11-23), two harness findings fixed. (1) Positional annotation text: native dispatch maps the second positional of comments, notes and learnings to add before validating output controls, so pm comments <id> \"text\" --output-limit 1 refuses read_output_mutation_conflict; the harness checked only options. annotationPositionalMutationOptions moved from src/cli/register-annotations.ts to src/sdk/read-output-contracts.ts (exported) and both the CLI preAction and the harness call it. (2) Order: native dispatch admits host output controls in preAction, before the action wrapper normalizes extension flags, so a non-read command given outputLimit and missing a required flag refuses read_output_surface_unsupported natively; the harness threw missing_required_option first. The harness admission now runs on the raw options before normalization. harness-parity.spec.ts covers both.\n"
  "2026-11-23T10:55:39.664Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 2 on PR #1772 (Codex and CodeRabbit, 2026-11-23). Harness admission now also sees option keys spelled as flags: '--add-json' and 'add-json' fold to addJson (a notes mutation option, so outputLimit beside it refuses read_output_mutation_conflict as natively), and '--output-limit' folds to outputLimit (refused on a non-read command). Folding uses resolveExtensionFlagOptionKey and only adds the folded key, so required-flag and value validation still run afterwards in normalization. harness-parity.spec.ts covers both spellings and an unfoldable short key.\n"
  "2026-11-23T11:57:25.823Z","harness:claude-code","Review round 3 on PR #1772 (Codex pass 3 and CodeRabbit, 2026-11-23). (1) Codex P2: dashed output controls were folded for admission only, so options { '--output-budget': '400' } on a read command was formatted without the budget; the folded canonical controls now also reach native formatOutput, so it refuses output_budget_exceeded like outputBudget does. (2) CodeRabbit: a declared short alias of a mutation flag (-J for --add-json on notes) was not folded for admission; folding now maps a key equal to a declared short spelling to its handler key. (3) CodeRabbit: docs now state that the refusal covers the output-shaping controls and that a renderer-only --output-format stays accepted (hasCanonicalReadOutputOptions excludes it). harness-parity.spec.ts covers (1) and (2).\n"
